We modify $P_i$ as follows: if $P_i = a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_{j_i}$, let $q_i$ be the last index such that $a_{q_i} \in X':= \{v_1, e_1, \ldots, v_c, e_c\}$ and let $p_i$ be the first index such that $a_{p_i} \in Y':=\{u_{\beta}, f_{\beta}, u_{\beta+1}, \ldots, f_{\ell}, u_{\ell}\}$. 

If $a_{p_i} =u_s$ for some $s$, then set $P_i'= P_i[a_{q_i}, a_{p_i}]$. If $a_{p_i} = f_s$ for some $s$, then set $P_i' = P_i[a_{q_i}, a_{p_i}], u_{s+1}$. 

Observe that $P_1'$ and $P_2'$ are either Berge paths or partial Berge paths in $H$. Moreover, $P_1'$ ends with vertex $z = u_{\beta}$
% or with $u_{i_1-1}$
and contains no other elements of $Y'$ since it is aligned  with $P'$. 
