Suppose not. If $h \in E(H')$, then $h$ contains a vertex outside of $\{u_{\beta}, \ldots, u_{\ell}\}$. But this violates either Claim~\ref{cXY} (B) or the definition of $S_1 = N_{H'}(u_{\ell}) \subseteq \{u_{\beta}, \ldots, u_{\ell}\}$. If $h = f_{g'}$, then $f_{g'} \in E(P'_2)$. By construction, $u_g=u_{g'+1}$, but in this case we chose $g'$ such that $g' < g-1$, a contradiction. This proves~\eqref{hdisjoint}.
 
